      "text": "To find the range of the function \\( f(x) = \\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} \\), we start by applying a property of the arctangent function. Specifically, we use the identity:\n\n\\[\n\\arctan a + \\arctan b = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{a + b}{1 - ab} \\right)\n\\]\nprovided that \\( ab < 1 \\), which is true in this case because \\(-1 < \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} < 1\\). Here, we have \\( a = x \\) and \\( b = \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} \\), so:\n\n\\[\nf(x) = \\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{x + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x}}{1 - x \\cdot \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x}} \\right).\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the expression inside the arctan:\n\\[\nx + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x(1 + x) + (1 - x)}{1 + x} = \\frac{x + x^2 + 1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x^2 + 1}{1 + x}.\n\\]\nTo simplify further, we recognize that:\n\\[\nx + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x^2 + x + 1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{(x + 1)^2 - x^2}{1 + x}(x - (1 - x)) = \\frac{(x + 1 - x)(x + 1 + x)}{1 + x} = \\frac{(x + 1)(2 + x - x)}{1 + x} = 2.\n\\]\nSo, we have:\n\\[\nf(x) = \\arctan 2.\n\\]\nHowever, this simplification is incorrect because we should have:\n\\[\nx + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x(1 + x) + (1 - x)}{1 + x} = \\frac{x + x^2 + 1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{x^2 + 1}{1 + x} = 1.\n\\]\nSo, the correct simplification is:\n\\[\nf(x) = \\arctan 1 + \\arctan 1 = \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n\\]\nHence, the only value in the range of \\( f(x) \\) is \\( \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\n\\]",
